{"status":"ready","content":"<think>\r\nLet me compute this determinant. Multiply each row by 6 to clear denominators, then divide by 6^4 = 1296.\r\n\r\nMatrix * 6:\r\nRow 1: 8, 6, -27, -26\r\nRow 2: -26, 25, -19, 11\r\nRow 3: -23, 29, -20, -19\r\nRow 4: -17, -7, 15, 14\r\n\r\nCompute det of this integer matrix, then divide by 1296.\r\n\r\nLet me expand along row 1 using cofactors. Actually, let me do row reduction.\r\n\r\nUse row 1 as pivot. R1: 8, 6, -27, -26.\r\n\r\nMultiply rows to eliminate. Let me use fractions.\r\n\r\nR2 = R2 + (26/8)R1 = R2 + (13/4)R1\r\nR3 = R3 + (23/8)R1\r\nR4 = R4 + (17/8)R1\r\n\r\nR2: -26 + (13/4)(8) = -26+26 = 0\r\n    25 + (13/4)(6) = 25 + 78/4 = 25 + 19.5 = 44.5 = 89/2\r\n    -19 + (13/4)(-27) = -19 - 351/4 = (-76-351)/4 = -427/4\r\n    11 + (13/4)(-26) = 11 - 338/4 = (44-338)/4 = -294/4 = -147/2\r\n\r\nR3: -23 + (23/8)(8) = 0\r\n    29 + (23/8)(6) = 29 + 138/8 = 29 + 69/4 = (116+69)/4 = 185/4\r\n    -20 + (23/8)(-27) = -20 - 621/8 = (-160-621)/8 = -781/8\r\n    -19 + (23/8)(-26) = -19 - 598/8 = -19 - 299/4 = (-76-299)/4 = -375/4\r\n\r\nR4: -17 + (17/8)(8) = 0\r\n    -7 + (17/8)(6) = -7 + 102/8 = -7 + 51/4 = (-28+51)/4 = 23/4\r\n    15 + (17/8)(-27) = 15 - 459/8 = (120-459)/8 = -339/8\r\n    14 + (17/8)(-26) = 14 - 442/8 = 14 - 221/4 = (56-221)/4 = -165/4\r\n\r\nNow det = 8 * det of 3x3:\r\n| 89/2   -427/4  -147/2 |\r\n| 185/4  -781/8  -375/4 |\r\n| 23/4   -339/8  -165/4 |\r\n\r\nFactor: multiply each row by stuff. Let me multiply row 1 by 4, row 2 by 8, row 3 by 8, dividing det by 4*8*8=256.\r\n\r\nRow 1 *4: 178, -427, -294\r\nRow 2 *8: 370, -781, -750\r\nRow 3 *8: 46, -339, -330\r\n\r\ndet of 3x3 = (1/256) * det of integer matrix.\r\n\r\nCompute integer 3x3 det:\r\n| 178  -427  -294 |\r\n| 370  -781  -750 |\r\n| 46   -339  -330 |\r\n\r\nExpand: 178 * [(-781)(-330) - (-750)(-339)] - (-427)*[370*(-330) - (-750)*46] + (-294)*[370*(-339) - (-781)*46]\r\n\r\n(-781)(-330) = 257730\r\n(-750)(-339) = 254250\r\nDiff: 257730 - 254250 = 3480\r\nFirst term: 178 * 3480 = 619440\r\n\r\n370*(-330) = -122100\r\n(-750)*46 = -34500\r\nDiff: -122100 - (-34500) = -87600\r\nSecond: -(-427)*(-87600) = 427*(-87600) = -37,405,200\r\n\r\n370*(-339) = -125430\r\n(-781)*46 = -35926\r\nDiff: -125430 - (-35926) = -89504\r\nThird: (-294)*(-89504) = 26,314,176\r\n\r\nSum: 619440 - 37,405,200 + 26,314,176\r\n= 619440 + 26,314,176 - 37,405,200\r\n= 26,933,616 - 37,405,200\r\n= -10,471,584\r\n\r\nSo 3x3 det = -10,471,584 / 256\r\n\r\nThen 4x4 (integer) det = 8 * (-10,471,584/256) = -10,471,584/32 = -327,237\r\n\r\nLet me verify: 10,471,584 / 32. 32 * 327000 = 10,464,000. Remainder: 7584. 7584/32 = 237. So 327,237. Yes.\r\n\r\nSo integer matrix det = -327,237.\r\n\r\nOriginal det = -327237 / 1296.\r\n\r\nSimplify: gcd(327237, 1296). 1296 = 2^4 * 3^4. 327237: odd. Divisible by 3? 3+2+7+2+3+7=24, yes. 327237/3 = 109079. 1+0+9+0+7+9=26, not divisible by 3. So gcd = 3.\r\n\r\n-327237/1296 = -109079/432.\r\n\r\nLet me check: 109079/432 ≈ 252.5. Hmm, let me double-check computation.\r\n\r\nLet me verify 178*3480. 178*3480 = 178*3000 + 178*480 = 534000 + 85440 = 619440. ✓\r\n\r\n427*87600 = 427*87600. 427*80000 = 34,160,000. 427*7600 = 3,245,200. Total: 37,405,200. ✓\r\n\r\n294*89504. 294*89504. 300*89504 = 26,851,200. Minus 6*89504 = 537024. = 26,314,176. ✓\r\n\r\nSum: 619440 - 37405200 + 26314176\r\n26314176 + 619440 = 26933616\r\n26933616 - 37405200 = -10471584 ✓\r\n\r\n-10471584/256: 256*40000=10240000. 10471584-10240000=231584. 256*900=230400. 231584-230400=1184. 1184/256=4.625. Hmm, not exact?\r\n\r\nWait, the 3x3 det should be 178/4 = ... let me recheck.\r\n\r\nActually 3x3 det (of fractional matrix) = (1/(4*8*8)) * (integer det). And 4x4 integer det = 8 * 3x3 fractional det.\r\n\r\nSo 4x4 = 8 * integer3x3 / 256 = integer3x3 / 32.\r\n\r\n-10471584 / 32 = ? 32 * 327237 = let me check: 32*300000=9600000, 32*27237 = 871584. Total: 10,471,584. ✓\r\n\r\nSo 4x4 integer = -327237.\r\n\r\nOriginal = -327237/1296 = -109079/432.\r\n\r\nHmm, let me double-check by computing 109079 = 327237/3. 3*109079 = 327237. ✓\r\n\r\n109079/432... Let me verify gcd. 109079 mod 2 = 1, odd. 109079 mod 3: 1+0+9+0+7+9=26, not div by 3. So gcd(109079,432)=1.\r\n\r\nAnswer: -109079/432.\r\n\r\nHmm let me double-check by an alternative approach. Let me recompute one of the eliminated rows to make sure.\r\n\r\nR2 = R2 + (13/4)R1 where original R2: -26, 25, -19, 11 and R1: 8, 6, -27, -26.\r\nR2[0]: -26 + 13/4 * 8 = -26 + 26 = 0 ✓\r\nR2[1]: 25 + 13/4 * 6 = 25 + 78/4 = 100/4 + 78/4 = 178/4 = 89/2 ✓\r\nR2[2]: -19 + 13/4 * (-27) = -76/4 - 351/4 = -427/4 ✓\r\nR2[3]: 11 + 13/4 * (-26) = 44/4 - 338/4 = -294/4 = -147/2 ✓\r\n\r\nR3 = R3 + (23/8)R1, original R3: -23, 29, -20, -19\r\nR3[0]: -23 + 23/8 * 8 = 0 ✓\r\nR3[1]: 29 + 23/8 * 6 = 232/8 + 138/8 = 370/8 = 185/4 ✓\r\nR3[2]: -20 + 23/8 * (-27) = -160/8 - 621/8 = -781/8 ✓\r\nR3[3]: -19 + 23/8 * (-26) = -152/8 - 598/8 = -750/8 = -375/4 ✓\r\n\r\nR4 = R4 + (17/8)R1, original R4: -17, -7, 15, 14\r\nR4[0]: -17 + 17 = 0 ✓\r\nR4[1]: -7 + 17/8 * 6 = -56/8 + 102/8 = 46/8 = 23/4 ✓\r\nR4[2]: 15 + 17/8 * (-27) = 120/8 - 459/8 = -339/8 ✓\r\nR4[3]: 14 + 17/8 * (-26) = 112/8 - 442/8 = -330/8 = -165/4 ✓\r\n\r\nGood. Now the 3x3 has rows (89/2, -427/4, -147/2), (185/4, -781/8, -375/4), (23/4, -339/8, -165/4).\r\n\r\nMultiplying row 1 by 4 (det *=4): 178, -427, -294\r\nMultiplying row 2 by 8 (det *=8): 370, -781, -750\r\nMultiplying row 3 by 8 (det *=8): 46, -339, -330\r\n\r\nSo integer3x3 det = 4*8*8 * frac3x3 det = 256 * frac3x3 det.\r\nfrac3x3 det = integer3x3 / 256.\r\n\r\n4x4 integer det = 8 * frac3x3 det = 8 * (-10471584)/256 = -10471584/32 = -327237.\r\n\r\nOriginal det = -327237/1296 = -109079/432.\r\n\r\nFinal answer: -109079/432.\r\n</think>\r\n\r\nLooking at this problem, I'll multiply each row by 6 to clear denominators (so the integer determinant must be divided by $6^4 = 1296$):\r\n\r\n$$M' = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 & 6 & -27 & -26 \\\\ -26 & 25 & -19 & 11 \\\\ -23 & 29 & -20 & -19 \\\\ -17 & -7 & 15 & 14 \\end{pmatrix}$$\r\n\r\n**Row reduction using $R_1$ as pivot:**\r\n\r\n$R_2 \\to R_2 + \\frac{13}{4}R_1$: $(0, \\frac{89}{2}, -\\frac{427}{4}, -\\frac{147}{2})$\r\n\r\n$R_3 \\to R_3 + \\frac{23}{8}R_1$: $(0, \\frac{185}{4}, -\\frac{781}{8}, -\\frac{375}{4})$\r\n\r\n$R_4 \\to R_4 + \\frac{17}{8}R_1$: $(0, \\frac{23}{4}, -\\frac{339}{8}, -\\frac{165}{4})$\r\n\r\nThe determinant equals $8 \\times$ (3×3 minor). Scaling rows by 4, 8, 8 (introducing factor 256):\r\n\r\n$$\\det\\begin{pmatrix} 178 & -427 & -294 \\\\ 370 & -781 & -750 \\\\ 46 & -339 & -330 \\end{pmatrix}$$\r\n\r\n**Cofactor expansion along row 1:**\r\n\r\n- $(-781)(-330) - (-750)(-339) = 257730 - 254250 = 3480$\r\n- $370(-330) - (-750)(46) = -122100 + 34500 = -87600$  \r\n- $370(-339) - (-781)(46) = -125430 + 35926 = -89504$\r\n\r\n$$= 178(3480) - (-427)(-87600) + (-294)(-89504)$$\r\n$$= 619440 - 37405200 + 26314176 = -10471584$$\r\n\r\n**Combining:**\r\n$$\\det(M') = \\frac{8 \\times (-10471584)}{256} = \\frac{-10471584}{32} = -327237$$\r\n\r\n**Original determinant:**\r\n$$\\det(M) = \\frac{-327237}{1296} = \\frac{-109079}{432}$$\r\n\r\n$$\\boxed{-\\dfrac{109079}{432}}$$\r\n","path":"responses/claude-opus-4-7/livebench-057-math.txt","size":6760,"mtime":1779367612}